.TH AX25D 8 "25 May 2015" Linux "Linux System Managers Manual"
.SH NAME
ax25d \- General purpose AX.25, NET/ROM and Rose daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ax25d [-v] [-c altconffile] [-l]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.LP
.B Ax25d
is a general purpose server daemon that listens on a number of AX.25, NET/ROM
and Rose ports and offers different services depending upon port, callsign
and other parameters.
.B Ax25d
is driven by a complex configuration file, a full description of which may
be found in another manual page.
.sp 1
.B AX25d
has the facility to log information about incoming connections to the
system log file. By default no logging is done. When
.B ax25d
is running, and a change in the configuration file is made,
.B ax25d
can be forced to re-read its configuration file by sending it a SIGHUP.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP 15
.BI "\-c altconffile"
Specifies an alternate configuration file name.
.TP 15
.BI \-l
Specifies that messages should be logged into the system log file. By default
no messages are logged.
.TP 15
.BI \-v
Display the version.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.LP
The program
.B ax25d
starts for a caller does
.B not
inherit the environment the daemon was started with: a service run for a
station on the air has no business seeing the sysop's shell.  The environment
is built here instead, and holds nothing but what is listed below.
.TP
.B AXSOCK_INHERIT
Who is at each end of the connection the child inherits on descriptor 0,
as
.IR "fd local peer" .
A child asking
.BI getpeername( 0 )
for the calling station \-\-
.BR axspawn (8)
does, before it picks a unix account \-\- gets AF_UNIX for an answer where the
connection is not a kernel socket.
.B libax25
reads this variable when it loads and answers for the descriptor, so no child
has to be changed.  See
.BR axsock (7).
.TP
.BR LD_PRELOAD ", " LD_LIBRARY_PATH
.RB ( DYLD_INSERT_LIBRARIES
and
.B DYLD_LIBRARY_PATH
on macOS) are passed on when they are set, and only these.  A station that
runs the userspace AX.25 shim by preloading it would otherwise lose it at
exactly this edge, and the child would find no AX.25 at all.
.SH FILES
.LP
/etc/ax25/ax25d.conf
